id: pm-ayg31c
title: "Typed-outcome reachability admits three of ten edge kinds, so the four semantic kinds the ontology exists to express contribute nothing to the invariant they were minted to satisfy"
description: "Typed outcome reachability currently evaluates only hierarchy and implements edges, so correctly modeled supersedes, discovered_from, verifies, and incident_from relations do not improve the invariant. Make the admitted kinds declarative, widen the basis with negative controls, and migrate its ratchets in one recorded step."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: governance,graph,measurement,ontology,reachability
created_at: "2026-08-13T08:33:42.357Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T18:38:40.635Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T18:03:00.671Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T18:03:00.671Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The set of edge kinds admitted by typed-outcome reachability is declared data rather than implicit in the governance implementation, and is reported alongside the reachability numbers; Every kind the ontology marks semantic can carry reachability, so supersedes, discovered_from, verifies and incident_from each contribute; An archived item joined to its replacement by the semantically correct kind is reachable, proven by the eleven canceled items currently counted unreachable; The basis change is measured as a delta on the existing reachability numbers, and the floors are re-declared over the new basis in one recorded step rather than drifting; A negative control proves the reachability score still falls when an item is genuinely disconnected, so widening the basis does not make the invariant unfailable"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "Every edge kind the ontology declares as semantic can carry an item to an outcome, so recording the correct relation is always sufficient"
value: "The project spent four waves minting typed edges specifically so lineage would be explainable. If the invariant that scores explainability ignores most of them, the incentive points back at hierarchy padding."
impact: "Eleven archived items are counted unreachable while carrying correct archival lineage, and 836 semantic edges are invisible to the reachability score that three governance assertions enforce."
outcome: "The reachability basis is declared, covers every semantic kind, and an item that records the semantically correct relation to living work is reachable through it."
why_now: "The reachability floors are now block-enforcement gates, so the narrow basis is actively steering enrichment toward the kinds that count."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Every relationship kind declared outcome-bearing contributes through its declared direction, the basis is reported, disconnected negative controls fail, ratchets enforce the migrated population, and the generated changelog carries the delivery."
actual_result: The registry declares traversal and outcome direction; governance reports and traverses the derived basis; all 2516 non-outcome nodes are reachable; zero are unreachable; basis score is 10000; strict controls pass; changed tests are linked through PM.
