comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T14:30:22.472Z","harness:claude-code","Decisive evidence for the basis claim, measured 2026-08-13 by recomputing reachability from the six outcome milestones plus pm-doxj over the on-disk edge set, parsing both TOON dependency encodings.\n\nOver the full edge basis every one of the 2,467 items reaches an apex: zero unreachable. Over the basis the governance code actually admits — parent, child, implements — exactly 11 do not: the eight canceled PRD-era epics pm-6hhn, pm-zetb, pm-murz, pm-met4, pm-xtfo, pm-gyfn, pm-defw and the archived duplicate pm-lty, plus the three canceled probe items pm-11ag, pm-crpv, pm-lql3.\n\nThe part that settles the argument: every one of those eleven already carries a correct, evidence-backed, recorded edge to a reachable node, and in every case it is a supersedes edge stored on the living side. pm-2xl supersedes pm-6hhn, pm-u9r supersedes pm-zetb, pm-c0r supersedes pm-murz, pm-54d supersedes pm-met4, pm-f45 supersedes pm-xtfo, pm-b1w supersedes pm-gyfn, pm-jiw supersedes pm-defw, pm-j7a supersedes pm-lty. The historical spine pm-1w6scp describes as missing is in fact present and correct in the data.\n\nSo the unreachable population is not a data gap and there is nothing to backfill. It is entirely an artifact of excluding one edge kind from the basis, and it is the specific kind whose semantics — this replaced that — is what a timeline query needs most. Recording that edge is the right modelling act and it moves the metric by zero, which is the strongest possible statement of this item's thesis: a project cannot improve a number the basis refuses to read.\n\nCorollary for the remedy. Widening the basis to include supersedes takes audit-basis unreachable from 11 to 0 without adding a single edge. That is worth doing before any further reachability ratchet, because a floor tightened against the narrow basis would permanently price in the exclusion."
  "2026-08-20T17:35:03.400Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-20: relationship-kind definitions now declare traversal family and typed outcome direction. Governance derives the basis entirely from the registry and reports it compactly as source_to_target=discovered_from,implements,incident_from,parent,recurs_from,verifies; target_to_source=child; both=supersedes. Live graph audit over 2,525 nodes and 12,450 edges reports zero findings, 2,516 non-outcome nodes reachable, zero unreachable, and 10,000 basis points for active, terminal, and total populations. Negative-control tests disconnect an item and prove the score falls, so widening the semantic basis does not make the invariant unfailable. Linked tests passed 44/44."
  "2026-08-20T17:36:10.440Z","harness:codex","Ratchet migration evidence: the three block-enforced assertions were updated through pm assurance put while retaining their canonical owners. graph-outcome-reachable-floor moved 2,438 to 2,516 with 2,515 as the failing control; graph-outcome-unreachable-ceiling moved 15 to 0 with 1 failing; graph-outcome-reachability-basis-points-floor moved 9,938 to 10,000 with 9,999 failing. The first attempt to transfer assertion ownership was correctly refused as a loosening, so the successful audited mutations preserve the existing owner lineage and name pm-ayg31c in their rationale."
  "2026-08-20T17:37:44.438Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification 2026-08-20: pnpm test:coverage passed 539 files and 7,644 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm quality:static passed generated contracts, SDK surface, package parity, grammar, token budgets, tracker context, graph composition, record integrity, and transport floors; ESLint passed with zero warnings; jscpd found zero clones across 1,067 files; docs links passed; secret scan found no credential-like material; pnpm audit found no known vulnerabilities. Manual acceptance used a disposable initialized tracker and verified semantic traversal, duplicate collapse without edge absence, malformed removal refusal, and typed zero-match recovery."
  "2026-08-20T17:39:10.298Z","harness:codex","Post-closure artifact evidence: pm-changelog 2026.8.17 regenerated CHANGELOG.md from 2,154 closed items using canonical main-branch PM links; the immediate package-owned check reported unchanged. Reopened solely to link this generated artifact before review."
  "2026-08-20T17:54:44.270Z","harness:codex","Hosted review remediation: Gates (static) correctly refused terminal defect work without escape_class and gate_evidence. Classified this as a production_defect and bound the fix to the declarative semantic reachability gate, its disconnected-item negative control, local assurance checks, and hosted static/coverage checks."
  "2026-08-20T18:02:59.834Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: linked all three changed reachability/registry test files through pm files. Extended the structural negative-control fixture so child explicitly exercises target_to_source outcome traversal, and updated the SDK metric docstrings to reference the declared outcome_reachability_basis."
  "2026-08-20T18:38:40.635Z","harness:codex","Operational closeout 2026-08-20: broad delivery PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1067 merged to main as ff1554259dccc6c161ae8353ef039d04e34f6a83. Exact merged-main CI run 32403253005 passed build, Windows, four coverage shards plus exact coverage aggregation, static/typecheck/compat/smoke gates, runtime smokes, and release-analyzer provenance; CodeQL, security/script quality, OSSF Scorecard, docs, and CodSpeed also passed. Same-day policy preserved the sole v2026.8.20 release; verify-published-release passed npm metadata, npx, bunx, pm-mcp initialization, bin coverage, and missing-bin negative controls. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with zero high/critical Sentry issues, 2.36% seven-day finish error rate, and zero missing error-code rows. Inline dogfood telemetry drained one queued event with queue_progressed=true and queue_empty=true."
